A||||3||RiceCooker||Heater Core - Q's & A's||||1||
Z||000000||RiceCooker||07-06-2001||11:33 AM||||Just wondering how many people have had to replace their heater cores.<P>I just replaced my second in less than two years so guess i would offer help to anyone that needs it. It's pretty simple but if you have any questions ask me.<P>Heater core is leaking when you can smell antifreeze in your car or when moisture comes out of your window defroster. It usually drips out of the casing in the passenger footwell (where people put their subs) When mine went the first time it was obvious cause antifreeze was running off of my CD Changer, and last i checked those things aren't intercooled.<BR>This time it was running out the back of the casing and soaking my underlay carpet. <BR>Oh well, got the old one out last night (minus some knuckles skin) and it sure was a POS. I'll put the new one in tonight and she'll be ready.<P>Cook'em<BR>Todd||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierojunky||07-06-2001||11:45 AM||||Mine went almost 2 years ago.  I didn't experience any leaking It just put this nasty film on the inside of the windows.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||PAUL88GT||07-06-2001||12:37 PM||||I just replaced the one in an 86se I am restoring. I acquired the car in February 2001 for a nominal fee. Anyhow, the heater core had been leaking so long that the carpet padding and carpet was saturated and moldy.  The smell in the car was terrible.  Since I was restoring the entire interior, I removed the passenger side carpeting and padding and pressure washed them both at the local car wash.  I also wiped the floor pan down with a mild bleach solution to kill the mold and mildew. Needless to say the car smells much better now.  I also had the dash out for repainting and this made changing the heater core and subwoofer speaker very easy. <BR>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by PAUL88GT (edited 07-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||07-06-2001||07:30 PM||||It lasted less than 2 years? was it used stock? For a new one to quit that fast....<P>You didn't have the right antifreeze mix in the thing. Very common problem. It should have been flushed then refilled to eliminate the old coolant.<P>The new one is defective. Happens. Is a big reason I stay with brands I know for these. <P>The car sat parked for extended periods. This lets the antifreeze settle leaving effectivily plain water at the top of the system. Then it's free to start coroding things...||||reg||1
